<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n83010" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πηρός</span></b>  (
			Dor.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πᾱρός</span> implied in <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔμπαρος, παρόω</span>, qq.v.), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ά</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>disabled in a limb, maimed</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ δὲ χολωσάμεναι πηρὸν θέσαν</span> [the Muses] made
			him <i>helpless</i> or <i>blind</i> (cf. <i><span class="en">
				Aesop.
				57
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				2.599
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πηρὸς ὁ μὲν γυίοις, ὁ δ᾽ ἄρ᾽ ὄμμασι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					9.11
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Phil.
			</span></i> or <i><span class="en">
				Isid.
			</span></i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πηραὶ τὰ σκέλεα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Mul.</u>
					2.131
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of the mind,
				<i><span class="en">
				Semon.
				7.22
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμβλεῖς καὶ π</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.624
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τῷ νῷ</span> Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pl.</u>
				48
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πηροὶ οἱ λογισμοί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Am.</u>
					46
				</span></i>
			.</div>
